<title>USA: California Financial Q1 EPS rises.</title>
<headline>California Financial Q1 EPS rises.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKTON, Calif. 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>California Financial Holding Co</p>
<p>(in thousands except per share)</p>
<p>								 Q1</p>
<p>							1997	    1996</p>
<p> Interest Income			    $ 25,201	 $ 23,577</p>
<p> Interest Expense			     14,742	   14,344</p>
<p>Net Interest Income After Provision</p>
<p>   for Losses on Loans			10,109	    8,968</p>
<p> Other Operating Income			1,757	    1,994</p>
<p> Other Operating Expense		     6,481	    6,578</p>
<p> Acquisition Related Costs		     661</p>
<p> Income Tax					2,036	    1,831</p>
<p> Net Income					2,688	    2,553</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share				.55		.54</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding</p>
<p>						 4,875,346	4,764,778</p>
<p>NOTE:  Q1 1997 included $660,000 in acquisition costs, the company said. Excluding these costs, earnings would have been $3.1 million of $0.64 per share.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
